1
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:16,380
Good morning, Susan.

2
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:23,030
Good morning, Sam.

3
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:27,390
What's the schedule today?

4
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:28,220
Ten o'clock,

5
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:30,550
telephone FAO Schwarz about the new twin baby dolls.

6
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:31,750
OK.

7
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:35,480
Telephone Mrs. Zaskey at the advertising agency.

8
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,620
I did that. Go on.

9
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:39,140
Eleven o'clock, approve the sketches for the toy spaceship.

10
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:40,190
Where are they?

11
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:41,750
Right here.

12
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,480
Did you look at them?

13
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,530
Yes, I did.

14
00:00:45,530 --> 00:00:47,770
What do you think of the spaceship?

15
00:00:47,770 --> 00:00:49,820
I think the kids'll love it.

16
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:56,150
Would you show me the drawings, please?

17
00:00:56,150 --> 00:01:01,380
Huh.

18
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:04,210
Now, what else is on the schedule today?

19
00:01:04,210 --> 00:01:05,750
Well, at one o'clock

20
00:01:05,750 --> 00:01:07,780
you have a lunch appointment with Mr. Levine,

21
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:09,710
the client from the Toytown Stores.

22
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:11,010
Where?

23
00:01:11,010 --> 00:01:12,470
At Rossano's.

24
00:01:12,470 --> 00:01:14,960
Hmm. Anything else?

25
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:15,930
At four o'clock,

26
00:01:15,930 --> 00:01:17,290
you have a meeting with the production staff

27
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:18,570
in the conference room.

28
00:01:18,570 --> 00:01:21,120
Make sure everybody is at that meeting.

29
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:22,380
Will do.

30
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:25,260
At six you're meeting, Mr. Ozawa.

31
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:27,500
Oh, yes. Are his models here?

32
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,430
They're in my office.

33
00:01:28,430 --> 00:01:29,200
I'd like to see them.

34
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,670
Right.

35
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:36,920
What else?

36
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,310
Come on, Sam ...

37
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:42,180
You work too hard, Susan.

38
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:44,650
When was your last day off?

39
00:01:44,650 --> 00:01:47,140
Hmm. I can't remember.

40
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:49,650
You really ought to take some time off.

41
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:50,740
What for?

42
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:54,340
To enjoy the simple things in life ...

43
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:56,490
I know, Sam.

44
00:01:56,490 --> 00:01:58,340
Maybe soon.

45
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:00,920
To smell the flowers.

46
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:04,560
Oh, wait a minute. What's today's date?

47
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:07,020
Today is the twelfth. Why?

48
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:14,280
It seems to me I scheduled something else.

49
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:17,130
There's nothing else in the appointment book.

50
00:02:17,130 --> 00:02:19,170
I'm sure I did.

51
00:02:19,170 --> 00:02:23,080
Oh, well, I'll probably remember it later.

52
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,560
I hope it isn't important.

53
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,670
Hmm. It's probably nothing.

54
00:02:26,670 --> 00:02:28,490
OK, let's get started.

55
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:31,920
Would you call Priscilla Smith at FAO Schwarz, please?

56
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:39,490
Right.

57
00:02:39,490 --> 00:02:41,950
These are the models from the Japanese film maker.

58
00:02:41,950 --> 00:02:46,890
Thank you. Just put them on my desk.

59
00:02:46,890 --> 00:02:51,450
And the new drawings for the toy spaceship.

60
00:02:51,450 --> 00:03:01,330
Wonderful.

61
00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:02,830
That was fast.

62
00:03:02,830 --> 00:03:03,900
We have a new artist.

63
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:05,430
She's very talented.

64
00:03:05,430 --> 00:03:06,780
What time is it, anyway?

65
00:03:06,780 --> 00:03:07,630
My watch stopped.

66
00:03:07,630 --> 00:03:09,430
It's eleven thirty.

67
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:13,040
What time is my lunch date with Bill Levine?

68
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:15,010
One o'clock.

69
00:03:15,010 --> 00:03:18,350
Remind me to leave at twelve forty-five.

70
00:03:18,350 --> 00:03:21,020
Did you remember your other appointment for today?

71
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:22,660
No,

72
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,960
but I have a feeling

73
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:39,010
it's going to be too late when I do remember.

74
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,810
Yes, Sam?

75
00:03:40,810 --> 00:03:43,880
I just solved the mystery.

76
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:45,120
What did I forget?

77
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:48,080
You have some guests in the reception room.

78
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,980
What? Who?

79
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,960
Mr. Harry Bennett and his daughter.

80
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:54,600
I remember!

81
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,170
Oh ... Harry!

82
00:03:57,170 --> 00:04:00,840
I made a lunch date with him and his daughter weeks ago.

83
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:04,820
Is he a client?

84
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:07,780
He's a friend.

85
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:11,380
Well, he's here with his daughter to have lunch.

86
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:12,860
I met her at Thanksgiving,

87
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:17,110
and I promised to have lunch with both of them today.

88
00:04:17,110 --> 00:04:18,880
Yes, indeed.

89
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:21,010
What are you going to do about your appointment

90
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:24,600
with Mr. Levine?

91
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:29,500
Any suggestions?

92
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:32,500
Oh!
